    intro: 'Every genuine spiritual tradition has understood that the inner life has a structure — that there are stages, thresholds, transformations, and arrivals on the path from ordinary consciousness to genuine awakening. The Gnostic tradition describes this structure with unusual precision, drawing on the great initiatic traditions of Egypt, Christianity, Buddhism, and Kabbalah to map a journey that, while demanding, is entirely possible for those who are willing to pay the price.',
