          'The broad road is the road of mechanical life: the path of least resistance, of following habitual patterns, of sleeping in the dream of the ordinary waking state. The narrow gate is the decision to work sincerely on oneself — to face what is actually there, to question what one has always assumed, to begin the patient work of inner transformation. It is "narrow" not because it is harsh but because it requires something real: genuine sincerity, genuine effort, genuine willingness to see.',
