          'The second and third mountains represent stages of development beyond ordinary human consciousness — the return into the Absolute after the path of initiation has been completed, and the path of the bodhisattva who chooses to remain in manifestation for the sake of all beings. These stages are described in detail in Samael Aun Weor\'s autobiography "The Three Mountains," and while they lie beyond the immediate horizon of most students, understanding the complete map gives the early work its proper orientation and dignity.',
